          "type": "turn",
          "question": "When someone says they have heart failure, does that mean the heart has stopped working?",
          "answer": "No. According to the general clinical reference on heart failure (condition-heart-failure), the name is misleading. It does not mean the heart has stopped or is about to stop. It is a long-term condition that is managed, often for many years.\n\nThe reference describes heart failure as a state where the heart cannot fill with blood or pump it out well enough to meet the body's needs. The heart is still working, but not as effectively as it should.\n\nThe passages I found did not cover what symptoms look like, how it is diagnosed, or how it is treated. A person with questions about their own situation could discuss them with their clinician.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
